RF.put("questb:b3",{"7123":{"id":7123,"t":"Speak with our Quartermaster","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the Frostwolf Quartermaster.","desc":"‹name›, the Frostwolf Quartermaster is looking for recruits, for tasks that lead into the mines of Alterac Valley. Speak with him; he will tell you more.\nFollow the road west into the bunker, then take the west exit and you'll find our quartermaster.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Hail, ‹name›! It is good to see a ‹class› like yourself, eager to do his part for the Horde. Speak with me again, for I have vital tasks for you...\nStart Jotek Alterac Valley End Frostwolf Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7123","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"643":{"id":643,"t":"Sigil of Arathor","lv":41,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Sigil of Arathor and return it to Zengu in Hammerfall.\nSigil of Arathor Lieutenant Valorcall","desc":"Though they can barely be said to control Stromgarde, let alone the whole of Arathi Highlands, the human prince trots the remnants of his cavalry over the countryside. I can't understand why he does it, but who understands the way the humans think, hm?\nWhatever his reasoning, more importantly, he has given one of the sigils to Lieutenant Valorcall, their cavalry leader. Locate him and bring his sigil back to me.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Valorcall will not be easy to track down, ‹name›. Mounted on horseback, he can cover ground quickly. Nonetheless, we must have his sigil.","done":"Losing their cavalry leader will prove a large blow to the Stromgarde defenders. Better yet, it means that we are only one sigil from being able to have Trol'kalar for ourselves.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1043":{"id":1043,"t":"The Scythe of Elune","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Look for signs of the Scythe of Elune then return to Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire.\nFind evidence of the Scythe of Elune","desc":"Your story rings true... I do not entirely understand your motives, but if your business here in Duskwood involves ridding the forest of worgen in any number, then I can forgo understanding for results.\nThere is a mine to the south that has been overrun with worgen... They appeared out of nowhere, but from what we know, that is where they first were found.\nGo about your business, but I would ask that if you find anything of import, you share it with me. We will accept any aid in our war against evil.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The woods are perilous for the unprepared. Keep your weapons close at hand and your wits even closer, or your next journey into the haunted forest may be your last.","done":"It is an interesting story you tell, ‹name›. Though the Carevin family's influence is not large enough that we might find the root of these troubles and finish them once and for all, we will do what we can to contain the worgens' numbers in Duskwood.\nAlready I have instructed Calor to make this his first priority.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":49,"n":"Jonathan Carevin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"723":{"id":723,"t":"Prospect of Faith","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Hammertoe's Amulet to Prospector Ryedol in the Badlands.\nHammertoe's Amulet Magregan Deepshadow\nProvided: Hammertoe's Amulet","desc":"<Hammertoe holds his wounds and takes a moment to regain his composure before speaking again.>\nFind Ryedol, ‹name›. Bring 'im me amulet. <cough cough> He'll... <cough> figure out what to do. He knows I was seeking the origins of our people, and he... <cough>... knows it was also my mission to stop the Shadowforge clan. They must not be allowed to find the scrolls... <cough>","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I'd say it was a bad day, but this is the Badlands: every day's a bad day.","done":"Hammertoe's amulet? I think my spirits were higher when I thought he was dead. Knowin' fer sure only makes the pain worse. This amulet was his life's work. I can't let his death be in vain.\nLoch Modan Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.3,"y":85.8,"n":"Hammertoe Grez","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":53.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Prospector Ryedol","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"6563":{"id":6563,"t":"The Essence of Aku'Mai","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Sapphires of Aku'Mai to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\n20 Sapphire of Aku'Mai Sapphire of Aku'Mai , Sapphire of Aku'Mai , Sapphire of Aku'Mai","desc":"Within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps, large sapphire clusters can be found along the cave walls. Recently it was noted that the naga were harvesting the crystals. Until it can be discerned why, I sense we should stop the naga from succeeding. The crystals have great elemental power and if used inappropriately, could make for a powerful arcane component.\nWill you help me, ‹name›? Blackfathom Deeps can be found along Zoram Strand to the north of our outpost.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+150 reputation with Earthen Ring","back":"How goes your search for the crystals, ‹name›? Have you witnessed the naga harvesting them? I pray to my ancestors we find the reason they are collecting such things.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. These are the crystals I spoke of. Intriguing...\nI can feel the power within them. The spirits of water cling to them. Whatever the naga were going to use these for... well, let us be glad they are no longer in their hands.\nAshenvale Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"4083":{"id":4083,"t":"The Spectral Chalice","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,650 experience instead of 575, 9.83 times as much.","obj":"2 Star Ruby Scholomance Student 7.7 % in Scholomance , Doomguard Commander 6.7 % , Dreamroarer 6.1 % , Living Storm 5.6 % and 4 more\n20 Gold Bar Tattered Chest 2 % , Battered Chest 0 % , Alliance Chest 0 % , Solid Chest 0 % and 4 more\n10 Truesilver Bar Felsteel Chest 8.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 5.1 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 5.1 % , Solid Chest 0 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"The gems make no sound as they fall into depths of the chalice...","done":"The spectral chalice floats in the air, slowing rising and falling... as if to the beat of a dying heart.\nStart Spectral Chalice End Spectral Chalice Level 55 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 51 53 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4083","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4003":{"id":4003,"t":"The Royal Rescue","lv":59,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Now open to both factions.","obj":"Slay Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and free Princess Moira Bronzebeard from his evil spell.\nEmperor Dagran Thaurissan slain","desc":"This strike against the Dark Iron dwarves, if successful, will send a shockwave throughout their entire kingdom.\nPrincess Bronzebeard is under the control of Emperor Thaurissan. To free her, you must kill the Emperor. Be warned, your task is doubly dangerous, as Bronzebeard will attack you without question while under the control of the Emperor.\nDO NOT HARM HER!","rew":"Experience: 8,050","back":"<Princess Moira cowers in fear.>","done":"What have you done!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"8963":{"id":8963,"t":"Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire a Starbreeze Village Relic and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nStarbreeze Village Relic Frostmaul Preserver , Frostmaul Giant","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nIsalien, our priestess, grew up in Winterspring at Starbreeze Village. I need you to gather a Starbreeze Village Relic from the Frostmaul giants of Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, who are known for raiding to the north from time to time.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the relic into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to go to the Shrine of Eldretharr in the east wing of Dire Maul, and use the brazier to summon forth the spirit of my former cohort, Isalien. Her spirit has been corrupted by her possession of the piece of Valthalak's amulet, and the portion of his soul within it.\nBurning Steppes Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"5283":{"id":5283,"t":"The Art of the Armorsmith","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To become an Armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Grumnus: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.\n4 Ornate Mithril Helm\n2 Ornate Mithril Boots\nOrnate Mithril Breastplate","desc":"So ye made the smart decision.\nThere ain't no love lost betwixt me an old Ironus here. That good for nothing toy maker knows who the true craftsmen round here be.\nThe truly great wars are won with a good defense. When it be go time, no offense is gonna be helping ye out.\nRight, so let's get to work. All ye need to do is show me that ye've got some raw talent. After that, I'll yank whatever impurities be left in ye and mold ye into an armorsmith. Ye do know how to make ornate mithril, don't ye?","rew":"You will learn: Armorsmith\nExperience: 3,150","back":"Ah, ain't nothing like a good forge tan. Ye can tell who's got the really good tans by their apron lines.","done":"This be it, ‹name›. After this, there ain't no way to turn back. It's not too late to become a toy maker, er, weaponsmith.\nI trust ye'll make the right decision.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.1,"y":28,"n":"Grumnus Steelshaper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"4483":{"id":4483,"t":"Libram of Resilience","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Black Diamond Borer Beetle 5.2 % , Dark Keeper Uggel 4.6 % , Crest Killer 3.8 % , Burrowing Thundersnout 3.6 % and 4 more\n4 Crystal Spire\nBurning Essence\nLibram of Resilience Dark Keeper Zimrel 0.9 % , Hahk'Zor 0.8 % , Stonard Grunt 0.6 % , Dark Keeper Vorfalk 0.5 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Arcanum of Resilience","back":"If it is resilience you desire, thirty gold I require.","done":"Other librams are lost in this world. Lost in places you would not dare enter. Places you would pray did not exist.\nI will drink in the energies of these components. You shall be given the residual waste...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.6,"n":"Mathredis Firestar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97923":{"id":97923,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Gelman Stonehand in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51,"y":17.2,"n":"Gelman Stonehand","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94243":{"id":94243,"t":"Craftsmans writ heavy quiver","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Heavy Quiver\nHeavy Quiver","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Heavy Quiver, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Need some work?","done":"I--Hmm.\nI don't remember why I ordered this.\n<Ziz shrugs and tosses the quiver into a nearby pile of junk.>","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94323":{"id":94323,"t":"Craftsmans writ major rejuvenation potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Major Rejuvenation Potion\nMajor Rejuvenation Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Major Rejuvenation Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Major Rejuvenation Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94323","cats":["crafting"]},"4723":{"id":4723,"t":"Beached Sea Creature","lv":13,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Creature Bones Beached Sea Creature\nProvided: Sea Creature Bones","desc":"The remains of a giant thresher - much larger than one you'd expect to find in Darkshore - lie beached on the coast of the Mist's Edge. How this creature came to be here is unknown; the group of murlocs that now feast off the carcass of it seem to be much too weak, even in large numbers, to have brought down the beast.\nWhile some of it has been picked clean, enough of it remains to take a sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to study.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›! Are you here to report on another discovery?","done":"The bones you have are from gentle sea mammals that are known to inhabit the waters surrounding the base of Teldrassil. They had never been known to violently beach themselves like the threshers had been known to. Why would these creatures do this, I wonder? Well, perhaps the study of their remains will bear the fruits of knowledge that we seek.\nAgain, thank you for your aid. Please accept this honorarium from the Temple of the Moon.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":41.9,"y":31.5,"n":"Beached Sea Creature","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"963":{"id":963,"t":"For Love Eternal","lv":16,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free the spirit of Anaya Dawnrunner and bring her pendant back to Cerellean Whiteclaw in Auberdine.\nAnaya's Pendant Anaya Dawnrunner","desc":"In the aftermath of the battles at the Well of Eternity, I heard that Ameth'Aran had been destroyed, its people dead, including my love, Anaya.\nI would never have thought, thousands of years later, that memories of Anaya would still haunt my dreams. Wandering the woods of Darkshore in a stupor, I found myself in the ruins of Ameth'Aran... where I saw the haunted spirit of my beloved.\nShe must be freed, but I lack the heart to do it. Her spirit must be destroyed.","rew":"You will receive:\nTear of Grief\nExperience: 875\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"With a great sorrow in my heart, I followed the Shan'do Stormrage into hibernation, and took my sorrow to my dreams, sleeping for the passing of thousands of years.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Perhaps it would have been better... if I had done it myself. But even after these thousands of years, I could not bear to raise my hand against my beloved.\nPlease, I would be alone with my grief...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":35.7,"y":43.7,"n":"Cerellean Whiteclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"3763":{"id":3763,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Staghelm","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Darnassus is looking for seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly in the Cenarion Enclave within Darnassus proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Well now, ‹class›... since you were informed that I was leading this research myself, you obviously came as quickly as you could.\nNow that you are here, be sure to pay attention the first time I tell you the details; I have no desire to repeat myself.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":67.4,"y":15.6,"n":"Innkeeper Saelienne","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"5763":{"id":5763,"t":"Hunting in Stranglethorn","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Roon's Kodo Horn to Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn.\nRoon's Kodo Horn\nProvided: Roon's Kodo Horn","desc":"Long ago, a dwarf came to this land. His name was Hemet and he wished to hunt great beasts. His skills with the rifle were uncanny, and we spent many days hunting together. Even the enmity between our peoples was forgotten.\nWhen he left Desolace for Stranglethorn, I vowed to one day welcome him back so that we may hunt again. Now is that time.\nTake this kodo horn as a gift to Hemet. He will know it is from me. You will find him in Stranglethorn, north of the Grom'gol Base camp.","rew":"Experience: 1,250","back":"Sit, ‹class›. Soon enough you'll strike back into the jungle.","done":"Ah, this horn belongs to a Tauren, Roon Wildmane. He and I had a good time hunting the beasts of Desolace. So Roon is inviting me back, is he?\nWe're neck deep in the jungle right now, but thank you, ‹name›. Perhaps my next expedition will take me back to Desolace, the land of the centaurs.\nDesolace Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":25,"y":72.3,"n":"Roon Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5923":{"id":5923,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Mathrengyl Bearwalker has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Mathrengyl is the direct assistant to the Arch Druid himself, and is one of the most sage and august druids you'll find in Teldrassil.\nHe is located in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus, on the second floor of Fandral Staghelm's tree.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.9,"y":61.6,"n":"Kal","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"403":{"id":403,"t":"Guarded Thunderbrew Barrel","lv":1,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"This barrel of ale is guarded by Jarven Thunderbrew. As long as he's in the basement, no barrels may be disturbed.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.7,"y":52.7,"n":"Guarded Thunder Ale Barrel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"98323":{"id":98323,"t":"Secure the mountain","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Mountaineer Gretchen's Report back to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.\nProvided: Mountaineer Gretchen's Report","desc":"Hopefully ye put down a fair number of the mongrels while you were in there. Shame about Cornelius, though.\nFrom what you described, there's not much to report other than the cave is a lost cause. Whitebeard's not gonna like that answer, but I'm not darin' sendin' anybody else into that death trap.\nFeel free tae pass along the message, ‹name›. I'm not leavin' this spot till the mountain's secure.","back":"Ah, you're back just in time.\nWhat's the matter, lad? You look like you've seen a ghost.","done":"Completely overrun? Why am I not surprised.\nWell, that's going in the report too.\n<Senir folds Gretchen's letter into his pile of notes>","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":44,"y":57,"n":"Mountaineer Gretchen","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Senir Whitebeard","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"5843":{"id":5843,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Valley of Trials Gift Voucher to Magga.\nValley of Trials Gift Voucher\nProvided: Valley of Trials Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Magga in the Valley of Trials. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Hello! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":43,"y":69.4,"n":"Magga","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"99123":{"id":99123,"t":"Lost in the shadows","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Help Pal'juh escape Kolkar Crag and bring news of your success to Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village.\nEscort Pal'juh out of Kolkar Crag.","desc":"I decided to do a bit of scouting in the crag on my own. Unfortunately my magic ran out at the wrong time and I've been stuck hiding here since.\nIf you could help me escape, I would appreciate it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKolkar Hammer Kolkar Bow\nExperience: 700","done":"Ah, Pal'juh got herself in trouble again, did she?\nHopefully she learns her lesson about going alone this time. Thank you for helping her. She's a promising hunter, just tends to act more like a raptor than a tiger.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.2,"y":78.6,"n":"Pal'juh","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":55.8,"y":74.4,"n":"Master Vornal","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"163":{"id":163,"t":"Raven Hill","lv":20,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find out what is haunting Raven Hill.","desc":"Something's amiss at Raven Hill, ‹name›. Calor swears that someone--or something--is haunting the buildings there. Two nights running he's noticed the shadows moving, and the third before that he says he saw light in one of the windows.\nIf, as you say, you care about the safety of Duskwood, find out what monster haunts in Raven Hill.","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"No! Please don't kill me! It's just me... Jitters!! They're everywhere... I can't escape them! Monsters in Raven Hill? N-n-n-o... couldn't be. Only harmless Jitters.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Elaine Carevin","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":18.4,"y":56.4,"n":"Jitters","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"79363":{"id":79363,"t":"Silvias sword","lv":26,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat 7 Defias Night Blades and 7 Defias Enchanters in Addle's Stead then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.\nDefias Night Blade slain : 0/ 7\nDefias Enchanter slain : 0/ 2\nProvided: Silvia's Sword","desc":"A sword left by the spirit of Raven Hill's guard, Silvia Valor, who lived her life protecting civilians and their homes.\nWith Silvia's spirit still visiting farmsteads, perhaps her unfinished business was to route the defias who have taken up residence in Addle's Stead south of Raven Hill.","back":"Wade into any danger yet?","done":"Shake dat sludge off, we almost done.\nAlterac Mountains Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"323":{"id":323,"t":"Proving Your Worth","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Skeletal Raiders, 3 Skeletal Healers and 3 Skeletal Warders, and then return to Sven.\nSkeletal Raider slain : 0/ 15\nSkeletal Healer slain : 0/ 3\nSkeletal Warder slain : 0/ 3","desc":"Morbent Fel is a necromancer, and an ally to the dark riders. I would pit you against the power of Morbent Fel, but I will not send you against that vile fiend without first knowing your strength.\nYou have already proven your bravery to me, but if you truly wish to face the necromancer, then you must now prove your skill against his minions.","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Battle hard, ‹name›. And do not despair, for despair is evil's greatest weapon.","done":"Your skill in combat, ‹name›, can not be doubted. Your resolve may yet see us through to the end of Morbent Fel!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1203":{"id":1203,"t":"Jarl Needs a Blade","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Swamp Ring.","obj":"Bring a Moonsteel Broadsword to Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh.\nMoonsteel Broadsword","desc":"I have cutting to do. I can't tell you what I'm going to cut, but... I need myself a blade. A certain blade...\nSome people call it a moonsteel broadsword. I call it a swing blade.\nYou help me? Maybe you find it in town, maybe you talk to a blacksmith and he'll make it special.\nBut don't sleep on this. What I'm cutting won't keep forever...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nReedknot Ring Swamp Ring\nNew in Forever: Swamp Ring.\nYou will also receive:\nArtisan's Trousers\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450","back":"You have my blade??","done":"That's a good blade. It has a good swing. It's a good swing blade. Thank you. Thank you, thank you, thank you!!! Now I want to try it....\nLater. I'll try it later. But like I was saying... thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":26.3,"n":"\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9203":{"id":9203,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Flask of Petrification","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 1 Flask of Petrification and the Craftsman's Writ - Flask of Petrification - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Flask of Petrification\nFlask of Petrification\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Flask of Petrification","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order AL-90:\n1 Flask of Petrification.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"No comment.\n<Packmaster Stonebruiser glares at you.>\nI said no comment! Now get out of my sight!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9123":{"id":9123,"t":"The Dread Citadel - Naxxramas","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will grant you Arcane Cloaking at no cost. You must be Exalted with the Argent Dawn.\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via a permanent arcane cloaking of sorts - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. With that said, the cloaking is costly; however, your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is unwavering! We will waive all cost associations.","back":"None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.","done":"You will feel a slight tingle, ‹name›. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"83":{"id":83,"t":"Red Linen Goods","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Red Linen Bandanas to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp.\n6 Red Linen Bandana Defias Dockworker 66 % , Defias Bodyguard 66 % , Defias Dockmaster 66 % , Surena Caledon 66 % and 4 more","desc":"The Defias gang in Northshire wears burlap masks, but the Defias in Elwynn wear linen which I can use to make fine linen goods.\nBring me red linen bandanas and I'll use them to fashion something for you.\nDefias gang members have camps pocketed throughout Elwynn.","rew":"You will receive:\nRed Linen Shirt Red Linen Sash\nExperience: 775\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I'm running low on linen, ‹name›. Do you have any for me?","done":"Ah, these are nice bandanas, if a little rough...\nHere you are!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":79.5,"y":68.8,"n":"Sara Timberlain","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3363":{"id":3363,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":63.9,"y":6.1,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4403":{"id":4403,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":45.4,"y":18.3,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5203":{"id":5203,"t":"Rescue From Jaedenar","lv":55,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Arko'narin to where Lightforge and her equipment are being held, and then protect her as you escape Shadow Hold. Afterwards, seek out Jessir Moonbow in Felwood to let her know what's happened to her friends.","desc":"But, as much as it pains me, there is one thing that must be done first: I have to find Trey's sword Lightforge and escape Shadow Hold to tell my superiors what's happening here. Can you help me, ‹name›?\nOur equipment isn't far from here, and you've already proven you can survive the path to the top.\nAfter we escape, I'll head to Darnassus if you can find my friend Jessir near the Ashenvale border. She was to meet us at the Emerald Circle's camp near there.\nWhat do you say, ‹name›? Can you help me again?","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"You look winded, ‹name›. Are you all right, or is something wrong?","done":"You were the one who helped Arko escape? I'm so glad you found me. She passed by here not too long ago on her way to Darnassus. She had Lightforge in tow and wouldn't even take time to speak to the druids to be healed. She said it was far too urgent.\nBut she did tell me about your encounter with Trey's spirit. What a terrible fate for a Knight of the Silver Hand. She didn't show it, but I know it's tearing her up inside, the thought of losing one of her closest friends.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":36.2,"y":55.5,"n":"Captured Arko'narin","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":82,"n":"Jessir Moonbow","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3123":{"id":3123,"t":"Testing the Vessel","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Hinterlands, and locate the Wildkin. Kill 10, and use the Muisek Vessel to shrink and capture the fallen Wildkin.\nBring 10 Wildkin Muiseks and the Muisek Vessel to Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Feralas.\n10 Wildkin Muisek\nWildkin Muisek Vessel\nProvided: Wildkin Muisek Vessel","desc":"This will be a test; both of the ritual I performed, and of your abilities. Take this vessel, ‹name›. With it, you will have the power to shrink and capture a creature inside of it.\nTravel to the Hinterlands and look for creatures known as Wildkin that were once pets of the night elf goddess Elune. The vicious, primitive, or savage owlbeasts are your targets, ‹name›. Kill 10, and use the muisek vessel to shrink and capture them before their spirits can escape.","rew":"Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to capture the wildkin?\nIf you succeed, we will be ready to shrink and capture the muisek of creatures of Feralas.","done":"Upon a violent death, the muisek of a creature may escape and seek revenge. Shrinking the creatures, as you did, ‹name›, prevents the muisek from escaping. Now we may use it as we please!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3843":{"id":3843,"t":"The Newest Member of the Family","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take your Fragile Sprite Darter Egg to the Hinterlands and speak to Agnar Beastamer, but hurry, you only have 1 hour to find him before the hatchling within the egg dies.\nFragile Sprite Darter Egg\nProvided: Fragile Sprite Darter Egg","desc":"A magnificent specimen, ‹name›. If this creature survives gestation, then it'll be a healthy pet indeed!\nThere is one last thing I would suggest doing if you plan on following through with this--head to Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands. Speak to a dwarf there named Agnar Beastamer, he's a master animal handler and should be able to guide you in the final steps of incubation.\nBut hurry, ‹name›, this egg is fragile and will not last long without proper care.","rew":"Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Greetin's, ‹name›. How can I be of service to ya?","done":"Well, well, well... I haven't seen one of these in a dragon's age. Faerie dragon, if I'm not mistaken... looks to be of the sprite darter variety. Excellent, excellent indeed.\nWell, if this little fella's gonna hatch and live to be strong and healthy, then we should get some food for it. Good ya got it to me in time.\nThousand Needles The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":74.7,"n":"Quentin","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.2,"y":43.6,"n":"Agnar Beastamer","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"563":{"id":563,"t":"Reassignment","lv":32,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Farren's report to Major Samuelson in Stormwind Keep.\nFarren's Report\nProvided: Farren's Report","desc":"It shouldn't be a problem getting my report seen. The new captain of the guard, Major Samuelson, was my mentor while I was stationed in Stormwind. It should give him more than enough excuse to have me transferred back to the city. I'll need you to carry my report to him, though... wouldn't want ol' Redpath to catch on.","rew":"Experience: 3,200","back":"Greetings, citizen. May the Stormwind city guard be of assistance?","done":"What's this? Ah... so my attentive pupil has applied himself to the problem of the naga in Southshore. Thank you for bringing this to me, I will certainly take it into account when I review personnel assignments in the next month.\nHillsbrad Foothills Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":75.8,"y":36.7,"n":"Major Samuelson","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6083":{"id":6083,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Surf Crawler. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Thotar at Razor Hill.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"The advantage a pet affords you against your rivals is duly noted, ‹name›. When you gain control over another creature, you are adding to your own strength. Your pet must become an extension of yourself.\nThe next task requires you to turn from the land; you will find the next creature in the waters off the coast. Across from Sen'jin Village, near the Echo Isles. look for a spirited crab called the surf crawler. Use the taming rod to tame it, then practice your skills.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"You need to practice in order to gain the skills you need to effectively control your pet. Have you tamed a surf crawler?","done":"You are a swift learner, ‹name›. You have done well.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"2963":{"id":2963,"t":"Portents of Uldum","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Historian Karnik in the Hall of Explorers within Ironforge.","desc":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Your discovery inside Uldaman has set the Explorers' League abuzz with excitement. The League has been working to unlock the secrets of the miniature platinum discs you found. Your fortuitous arrival here in the Hall allows me to share with you that we are quite possibly on to something!\nHistorian Karnik has uncovered some important clues as to the true origins of the Valley of the Watchers in the Tanaris desert. He would like to speak with you as soon as possible!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","done":"I am glad you're maintaining your interest in exploration, ‹name›! With your natural talent and moxie, we could crack open secrets that we never thought were possible!\nThe Discs of Norgannon in Uldaman were a repository of vast information; you were only permitted to access the top layers, as it were, of the information stored there. The Creators were rumored to have more repositories located throughout Azeroth. This now brings us to Uldum...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.1,"n":"High Explorer Magellas","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8643":{"id":8643,"t":"Highpeak the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":50,"y":48,"n":"Elder Highpeak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8723":{"id":8723,"t":"Nightwind the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":37.6,"y":53,"n":"Elder Nightwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8883":{"id":8883,"t":"Valadar Starsong","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use your Lunar Festival Invitation in the moonlight to travel to Moonglade. Speak with Valadar Starsong in Nighthaven when you arrive.","desc":"Now that you have your Lunar Festival invitation, you may travel to Moonglade! There you will find many revelers, and in the village of Nighthaven Valadar Starsong and his sister Fariel await those eager to participate in the celebration.\nTravel to Moonglade through the greater moonlight and speak with Valadar Starsong; see what prizes you might gain during the festival!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"‹name›, welcome to Nighthaven, host of the Lunar Festival! Although our village is normally remote and sequestered from the peoples of Azeroth, during this time of celebration we open our arms and hearts to all.\nEnjoy your visit, ‹name›, and speak with me or my sister again when ready.\nTirisfal Glades Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"6643":{"id":6643,"t":"Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Fiery Core","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fiery Core Firewalker 42.2 % , Flameguard 34.7 % , Firelord 23.4 % , Molten Destroyer 14.9 % and 1 more","back":"Woe unto those that tempt fate inside the Molten Core. Death comes swiftly - the punishment dealt without mercy.\nMany of the Brotherhood have been lost in their search for Fiery Cores.\nOffer 1 Fiery Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.","done":"Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\nStart Lokhtos Darkbargainer End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6643","cats":["molten-core"]},"9043":{"id":9043,"t":"Redemption Tunic","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Redemption Tunic if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Tunic, 25 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Tunic\n25 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Tunic\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Tunic.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3523":{"id":3523,"t":"Scourge of the Downs","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you agree to aid Belnistrasz, speak with him again and hand the Oathstone he gave you back to him.\nBelnistrasz's Oathstone\nProvided: Belnistrasz's Oathstone","desc":"Outstanding! My name is Belnistrasz, and I thank you for rescuing me. I had given myself up for dead... or worse, as a meal for these Scourge-infested vermin. Yes - I said Scourge all right; they've brokered some sort of deal with the Quilboar here, and this nightmare is a result.\nListen... rather than just flee, I want to make a difference for all of our sakes. Would you be up to helping me out to that end? It's probably dangerous, but you seem to be the type not to worry about that too much.","rew":"Experience: 290","back":"I'm not one for politics; I care not if your affiliations are for either Horde or Alliance. I am more interested in squelching direct and dire threats to all the races... and we have quite a large one in here.\nIf you're willing to be a true hero for all people, then hand me the oathstone I have given you as a sign of commitment. I'm... not from around these parts; an oathstone is important to people of my kind as a bond of agreement.","done":"Fantastic, I thought you looked to be the heroic type! We've got our work cut out for us ‹name›, I'm not going to lie to you. If we stay focused on the task at hand, we should be able to come out on top.\nNow, let me bring you up to speed on what's been going on...\nStart Belnistrasz Razorfen Downs End Belnistrasz Razorfen Downs Level 37 , requires level 32 Difficulty 32 33 35 40 47 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 3523\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 37, 4,540 XP in all.\n1 [ 37 ] Scourge of the Downs this quest\nIf you agree to aid Belnistrasz, speak with him again and hand the Oathstone he gave you back to him.\nBelnistrasz Razorfen Downs\n290 XP\n2 [ 37 ] Extinguishing the Idol\nEscort Belnistrasz to the Quilboar's idol in Razorfen Downs. Protect Belnistrasz while he performs the ritual to shut down the idol.\nBelnistrasz Razorfen Downs\n4,250 XP","cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"92483":{"id":92483,"t":"At home in the shadows","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Simple Note then speak with Akeri Duskblade within the watchtower in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Simple Note","desc":"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident rogue trainer--Akeri Duskblade--has requested to speak with you. He left this note, so read that first, then seek him out inside the watchtower, here in the village.\nHe's a shady fellow, but then again, so are you. I think you'll get along well.","back":"<Akeri eyes you suspiciously.>","done":"I almost did not hear you approach me, young ‹class›.\nAlmost.\nAlmost won't be good enough when you leave Thendal Grove. You must be a slender blade, silent and steady. Ever vigilant and ever mindful of your surroundings. You might have what it takes to survive the dangers of Zephras. You also might end up with your throat slit in a ditch. Ultimately that's entirely up to you.\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":24.2,"n":"Akeri Duskblade","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3443":{"id":3443,"t":"Forging the Shaft","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Thorium Plated Daggers to Kalaran Windblade.\n8 Thorium Plated Dagger Dark Iron Watchman 80 % , Dark Iron Lookout 80 % , Dark Iron Sentry 80 % , Dark Iron Taskmaster 80 % and 4 more","desc":"To hold the flawless flame, we will need a shaft and a casing. You must first find a suitable shaft.\nThe Dark Iron taskmasters and slavers of the cauldron use weapons of enchanted thorium, an extremely sturdy alloy. If you bring me eight thorium plated daggers, I can break the alloy down and reforge a shaft.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400","back":"Eight, ‹name›. I need eight!","done":"You're an exceptional laborer, ‹name›. Have you ever considered a change of vocation? Perhaps a detective? Junk collector? Oh, I know, one of those silly gnomes that crawl across the beaches of Azeroth with their metal detecting contraptions, looking for lost treasure. Yes, that would be an ideal position for you.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8803":{"id":8803,"t":"A Festive Gift","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFestive Gift","done":"The note on this present reads:\nTo ‹name›,\nIn hoping this will help you spread warm tidings and holiday cheer to all of Azeroth.\nFrom Greatfather Winter\nDun Morogh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.7,"n":"Festive Gift","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.4,"y":69.3,"n":"Festive Gift","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"6963":{"id":6963,"t":"Stolen Winter Veil Treats","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the Smokywood Pastures investigator that has gone missing in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"Listen... not to shatter the magic of the season here, but Smokywood Pastures could use some assistance - the kind you adventuring types are known to give.\nWe're missing an important shipment of treats that was restocking us for the season, and now we're missing the agent of Smokywood Pastures that we sent out to the field to find it! Please - the shipment was last reported in the Alterac Mountains, and that's where our man went to look for it.\nSee if both are out there, safe and sound!","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+50 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","done":"Y-y-you can h-h-hear me! Thank the b-b-bottom line!\nI'm not really a s-s-snowman - my n-n-name is Sacks, and I w-w-work for the Orgrimmar b-b-branch of Smokywood Pastures... I g-g-got sent out here to look for a m-m-missing package, when I was attacked by a c-c-creature I have never seen b-b-before!\nSo v-v-very cold...\nOrgrimmar Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":35.4,"y":72.5,"n":"Strange Snowman","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7043":{"id":7043,"t":"You're a Mean One...","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 35.","obj":"Locate and return the Stolen Treats to Wulmort Jinglepocket in Ironforge. It was last thought to be in the possession of the Abominable Greench, found somewhere in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.\nStolen Treats The Abominable Greench","desc":"A c-c-creature called \"The Abominable Greench\" is the one w-w-who stole our shipment of t-t-treats, ‹name›. Be c-c-careful though! He is t-t-the one who turned me into this s-s-snowy mess!\nYou're g-g-gonna need some help in f-f-facing him. I've seen him w-w-wander all around where the y-y-yeti are; he's s-s-surely here s-s-somewhere! F-f-find the treats ‹name›, take them b-b-back to Smokywood Pastures in Ironforge, and t-t-tell them I n-n-need to be unfrozen!","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"‹name› - our Feast of Winter Veil will be ruined without those treats to restock! Graccu himself will miss out on sharing his delicious meat pies with all the good boys and girls this season...","done":"You found it! You've saved Smokywood Pasture's Feast of Winter Veil!\nPoor Sacks... we'll be sure to send a team out there and figure out a way to unfreeze him. Hopefully, he'll be back in time for the day of the Feast; he'll need to make up missed time working though. Still, this wouldn't even be possible if it weren't for you!\nAlterac Mountains Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":35.4,"y":72.5,"n":"Strange Snowman","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.9,"n":"Wulmort Jinglepocket","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"96243":{"id":96243,"t":"Call of earth","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Teo Hammerstorm in Dun Morogh.","desc":"It's past time ye heeded the earth, brave Shaman. The elements already prickle in yer skin, but once ye speak with the stone, the ground itself'll set firm 'neath yer soles--and in yer soul.\nSeek out Teo Hammerstorm, in Coldridge Valley. Ye'll find him within Anvilmar, a holdfast forged by hammer, fire, and will.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.4,"y":52,"n":"Ingrid Dunwald","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1523":{"id":1523,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.","desc":"Long has it been since you were last tested, ‹name›. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about destruction... and chaos. The element of fire is yours for the understanding, if you're prepared to pay for it.\nSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the night elf lands, you've gone too far.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Hmmm, Narm sent you to me, did he?\nWell then, Narm could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.\nI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, ‹name›. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22,"y":18.8,"n":"Beram Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8323":{"id":8323,"t":"True Believers","lv":59,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hermit Ortell wants you to bring him 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts\n10 Encrypted Twilight Text Twilight Prophet , Twilight Marauder 25 % , Twilight Marauder Morna 25 % , Twilight Overlord 25 % and 4 more","desc":"Now that I have the Twilight Lexicon in my possession, there is a small favor I'd like to ask of you.\nMy former organization has a secret encoded bulletin they circulate on a monthly basis.\nIf they make any progress searching for me or if they call off the search, word will be published on the True Believer.\nAlthough this information is obviously valuable to me, the publication contains other useful information that I can share. Bring me any encoded texts you find on Twilight's Hammer members.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400","back":"Did you find any encrypted texts? I'm quite curious to read this month's True Believer.","done":"Excellent! I will get to decoding these as soon as possible. If I find anything of interest I'll find some way to get the information to you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":67.2,"y":69.8,"n":"Hermit Ortell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"6323":{"id":6323,"t":"Ride to the Undercity","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a bat ride to the Undercity from the bat master Karos Razok, then take Podrig's Order to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity.\nPodrig's Order\nProvided: Podrig's Order","desc":"One of my bats can take you to the Undercity, for a small fee. Speak with me again when you are ready so that we may arrange your transport.\nYou will find Gordon Wendham in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity. That is the same quarter where my bat will land.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"I keep my weapons in top condition. They are cleaned and ready for use.","done":"An order from the Sepulcher? Very well. It is an honor to serve those who serve our Dark Lady.\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":45.6,"y":42.6,"n":"Karos Razok","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":61.5,"y":41.8,"n":"Gordon Wendham","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1363":{"id":1363,"t":"Mazen's Behest","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Acolyte Dellis in Stormwind.","desc":"As caretaker of the works here in the library of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences, it is my responsibility to ensure all the magical tomes and scrolls are accounted for at all times. Who knows what folly would unfold if some of these enchanted texts were to fall into the wrong hands?\nWhich reminds me... my assistant, Dellis, made a horrible mistake last week. He's quite able in the library but incompetent when he leaves the gates of Stormwind. Be a hero, and help old Dellis out, would you?","rew":"Experience: 330\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"It wasn't my fault. Really it wasn't.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":74.2,"n":"Mazen Mac'Nadir","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.4,"y":73.8,"n":"Acolyte Dellis","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"6403":{"id":6403,"t":"The Great Masquerade","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Follow Reginald Windsor through Stormwind. Protect him from harm!","desc":"It has been quite the adventure, friend. I owe you a great debt of gratitude. Perhaps, when all is said and done...\nAs you have no doubt ascertained by now, Lady Prestor is Onyxia: Brood of Deathwing, twin to the tyrant of the Spire, Nefarian.\nFor too long she has held our kingdom in her captivating gaze. Even the Highlord is controlled by her trickery - a puppet. It all ends today... The spell will be broken.\nWorry not, for together, we shall be victorious!\nAre you ready?","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I... I... I was powerless.","done":"<Bolvar holds the shattered medallion.>\nThe magic held within must be reignited. The dragon's eye must be attuned.\nWindsor's sacrifice has freed our Kingdom, but the threat of Onyxia and her kin is ever looming.\nThis medallion is what held my mind and body captive. It is also what gave me access to Onyxia's own mind - to her secrets. Albeit the visions are muddled now, some things I do remember.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8243":{"id":8243,"t":"Zanza's Potent Potables","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Zandalar Honor Token\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSheen of Zanza Spirit of Zanza Swiftness of Zanza","back":"With your increased status amongst the tribe comes access to some of our more potent potables. Behold... these brews are strong in the mojo - blessed by Zanza and fit for adventurers from all walks of life!\nI will allow you to choose one from the three I offer; in exchange, I require three Zandalar Honor Tokens. Note that only the effects of a single one may course through your spirit at any given time.","done":"A fair trade, my friend - please enjoy the blessings of Zanza with our compliments!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.1,"y":16,"n":"Rin'wosho the Trader","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"6163":{"id":6163,"t":"Ramstein","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and slay Ramstein the Gorger. Take his head as a souvenir for Nathanos.\nHead of Ramstein the Gorger Ramstein the Gorger","desc":"I was overwhelmed. On this very stead, I stood... held my ground in defense of Lordaeron. The farm and all on it were waylaid by a gigantic wave of Scourge.\nThe wretch. The filth. It hovered above me, entrails hanging from its gaping chest cavity.\nI woke as Scourge. For so long I was helpless. My mind had coalesced with the Lich King's.\nShe came for me... somewhere, somehow, I knew she would. Free.\nAnd now, I must have my vengeance - my vengeance on that which took from me my life. Destroy it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRoyal Seal of Alexis Elemental Circle\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"After Sylvanas freed me, I hunted the beast across these wastes for months. It fled to the safety of Stratholme. The bastard...","done":"I wonder... did it beg for mercy? Could it know what mercy is?\n<Nathanos spits.>\nI will hang this beast's head upon my wall.\nYou have earned a spot amongst one of my champions, ‹name›.\n<Nathanos salutes.>","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"243":{"id":243,"t":"Into the Field","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan about getting a power source for the testing kit.\nProvided: Field Testing Kit","desc":"You will be headed to the Tanaris desert, testing the tissue consistency of the basilisks, scorpids, and hyena native there. Obtain tissue samples and use them with the testing kit in tow; expect a chunk of the samples to fail. I need eight acceptable samples of each creature type.\nIn addition, the goblins of Gadgetzan have a power source that must be used with this kind of modified kit. Speak to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle and acquire one for the kit.\nReturn to me only when you are successful.","rew":"Experience: 2,000\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ah, our model 4711-FTZ power sources! We normally use them to power the water wells, but THANKS TO THE VILE NOMADS, we have an over abundance of power sources right now.\nSure, I can get you a power source for whatever nefarious science experiment you think you're trying to hide from me. It ain't gonna be free though, ‹race›. Nothing's free in Gadgetzan.\nUndercity Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"483":{"id":483,"t":"The Relics of Wakening","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Relics of Wakening and bring them to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.\nRaven Claw Talisman Chest of the Raven Claw\nBlack Feather Quill Chest of the Black Feather\nSapphire of Sky Chest of the Sky\nRune of Nesting Chest of Nesting","desc":"Gnarlpine invaders were seen ravaging the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to the west.\nThe slumbering druids will be trapped in the Emerald Dream for eternity, unaware of their fate, unless we help. The delicate hibernation ritual cannot be broken without the Relics of Wakening.\nJourney to the Den and retrieve the Raven Claw Talisman, Black Feather Quill, Sapphire of Sky, and Rune of Nesting. The druids store them in sacred chests. Return them to me and I will prepare the awakening ritual.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBarkmail Leggings Gritroot Staff\nMoney: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, the kidnapped Druids of the Talon will be forever trapped in the Emerald Dream if we cannot retrieve the Relics of Wakening from the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to the west.\nFor every minute we delay their fate comes one step closer to eternal doom.","done":"You have succeeded, young ‹class›! Well done. And just in time I might add.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":57.3,"n":"Athridas Bearmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"98403":{"id":98403,"t":"Twisted hatred","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 8 Befouled Webwoods and bring Xethorr the Wicked's Mature Fel Moss to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.\nBefouled Webwood slain : 0/ 8\nMature Fel Moss","desc":"Lord Melenas did not act alone; he was at the behest of another. The one you seek is Xethorr the Wicked. It seems he has twisted the spiders that call Teldrassil home, intending their venom for some foul plan.\nHe has taken residence deep in the forest, in the area to the northwest of here known as the Cleft. Take caution, and bring allies, for Xethorr is not an opponent to be trifled with.\nDispatch his brood, and bring me anything that may tell us more of the satyr's work here.","rew":"You will receive:\nWebwood Slicer\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"<Tallonkai lowers his voice.>\nDoes Xethorr still walk freely?","done":"I should have known this was being used to twist the spiders of this land.\nI have heard whispers of this substance being the source of much of the corruption plaguing us. Though this is not the original, it is an older sample and may yield more information than what we have obtained so far.\nNormally I would have you send this to Darnassus for further study. However, it is best we kept this quiet for the moment, or Dolanaar will never recover its reputation.\nI trust you to do the same.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.4,"y":56.8,"n":"Tallonkai Swiftroot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"3923":{"id":3923,"t":"Rilli Greasygob","lv":18,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Broken and Battered Samophlange to Rilli Greasygob in Orgrimmar.\nBroken and Battered Samophlange\nProvided: Broken and Battered Samophlange","desc":"Well, that didn't work. I put some extra gauges on the samophlange to measure its structural integrity, and they read the integrity at an all-time low. I could add some more dials and maybe a lever or two to try and fix it, but... I think that might make things even worse.\nYou should take the samophlange to Rilli Greasygob. He used to work for the Venture Company -- if anyone knows how to fix it, it's Rilli.\nYou can find him at Nogg's Machine Shop in Orgrimmar, in the Valley of Honor.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Ratchet\n+10 reputation with Horde","back":"Mind your head! I don't want it to get in the way of my work!","done":"What's this? Why, it's a samophlange! Where did you get this thing? Have you been poking around the Venture Company holdings in the Barrens?\nYou must be very brave, or very stupid.\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.1,"y":11.2,"n":"Wenikee Boltbucket","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":76.5,"y":24.4,"n":"Rilli Greasygob","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5043":{"id":5043,"t":"Agamaggan's Agility","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Agamaggan's Agility","back":"My tribes greatest scouts are said to be unrivaled in their accuracy, and no rogue <snort> could measure up to their quickness in battle.\nBring me 4 blood shards and I will make you even more agile than any quilboar born.","done":"May your aim be unerring, and the mark of your weapon be true, ‹race›.\nAgamaggan's spirit is with you. Return <snort> to me if you wish. Mangletooth will bless you again if the great boar god deems me worthy. <snort>","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"883":{"id":883,"t":"Lakota'mani","lv":22,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Hoof of Lakota'mani to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.\nHoof of Lakota'mani Lakota'mani\nProvided: Hoof of Lakota'mani","desc":"The Hoof of Lakota'mani is a symbol of the strength of the great kodo.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, when you approached I saw a new power in your stride. Tell me -- has your spirit met with the great Lakota'mani?","done":"Lakota'mani is called Earthshaker in our language, and his steps are like gathered thunder. He is with you now, and his courage mingles with yours. Together there is no conflict you cannot face.\nWalk tall, ‹name›. Walk tall, Earthshaker.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"96403":{"id":96403,"t":"Important Heirlooms","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Collect 8 Dwarven Heirlooms from the Hall of Thanes.\n8 Dwarven Heirloom","desc":"You there, adventurer... I could really use your aid.\nI was sneaking--uh... 'patrolling' in the vaults when a force of Dark Iron dwarves emerged from the depths in mole machines! I don't know what they are here for, but there is priceless loot--uh or, rather... I mean, 'important cultural heirlooms' down there! Please, recover any such relics you see and return them here.\nI assure you that anything you recover will be catalogued and returned to its proper place of honor.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Tome Tomb Robber's Gloves\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,950\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"<Thom appears to absentmindedly rub his hands together as he looks at you.>","done":"Look at you, as brave as you are enterprising! I'm a gnome of my word, and your reward is well earned!\nNow, let me take a look at the haul--uh, I mean... the recovered heirlooms. I need to get started appraising--excuse me, 'cataloging' them so that they can be put back in their proper places as quickly as possible.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":32.4,"y":44.8,"n":"Thom Filch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hall-of-thanes"]},"7843":{"id":7843,"t":"The Final Message to the Wildhammer","lv":50,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Otho Moji'ko at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to travel to Aerie Peak in the western region of the Hinterlands and place the Final Message to the Wildhammer by the well in the center of town. Return to him once this task is complete.\nBeware of angry Wildhammer dwarves and unruly members of the Alliance.\nProvided: Final Message to the Wildhammer","desc":"<Otho hands you a long, blood drenched spear, wrapped in several gryphon feathers.>\nYou take this, mon. You take this to Aerie Peak, dead center of town by the well. You plant it! Drive it right into the ground! Show those dwarves that troll mean business! Come back when you do this. Hopefully you come back alive.","rew":"You will receive:\nOwlbeast Hide Gloves\nMoney: 2 20 2 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,900\n+200 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"What's the hold up, mon?","done":"I wish I coulda been there to see the look on their faces, mon. Are they packing up their bags? Leavin' town?\nYou done good, ‹name›. Real good. Otho reward you with the big mojo.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.4,"y":79.1,"n":"Otho Moji'ko","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1123":{"id":1123,"t":"Rabine Saturna","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade. Moonglade lies between Felwood and Winterspring, accessible through a path out of Timbermaw Hold.","desc":"For this task, Keeper Remulos' majordomo in Moonglade - Rabine Saturna - seeks aid in exploring the vast wastelands far to the west of Tanaris and Un'Goro. He is located in Nighthaven, the main village of Moonglade.\nI want to impart on you the importance of your presence. There are growing tensions between the night elves of Darnassus and the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade. Look beyond racial boundaries and tap into the wisdom of your ancestors in dealings with the Circle there, ‹name›. Good luck.","rew":"Experience: 1,400\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am Rabine Saturna, and on behalf of Keeper Remulos and all of the denizens of this sacred glade I bid you welcome.\nI appreciate your interest and eagerness to assist the Cenarion Circle. The tauren have shown an incredible propensity to the tenets of Cenarius, and by their proxy the Horde is welcomed within the safety of this glade. The preservation of Azeroth is a common goal we both share.\nYou are among friends here, ‹name›.\nThunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"4243":{"id":4243,"t":"Chasing A-Me 01","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater.","desc":"Unfortunately, something's happened to one of my greatest inventions. You've seen mechanical squirrels, yes? Well, to get closer to the apes of Un'Goro Crater, I created a mechanical ape to blend in with their kind--I call her A-Me 01.\nShe has scrying gems for eyes so I could see everything she saw. She made it to Fungal Rock--the apes' lair--just east of here, and that's when I lost contact. The last thing I saw was one of their alpha males rushing up to say hello to her!\nCan you help me find her?","rew":"Experience: 2,650","done":"As you look A-Me 01 over, you see two huge dents tarnishing what Karna obviously feels is a well-crafted piece of engineering. One dent decorates A-Me 01's shoulder, the other is on her head.\nNo power seems to be running through her components as you investigate further.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":46.4,"y":13.4,"n":"Karna Remtravel","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":67.7,"y":16.8,"n":"A-Me 01","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"65603":{"id":65603,"t":"The binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Using the Wooden Figurine, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Wooden Figurine to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.\nSummoned Incubus slain\nProvided: Wooden Figurine","desc":"The time has come. Take the figurine and descend into the crypts below. A summoning circle has been prepared, and you must place the figurine at its center.\nThen the gateway will open, and the incubus will cross into our world.\nA sayaad is not to be underestimated. The demon will not hesitate to attack when it realizes your ruse. You must draw upon all you have been taught to defeat it.\nIf you succeed, return to me and I shall bind the creature to your will. Fail, and your soul is forfeit.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nExperience: 1,150","back":"The incubus will try to lower your guard through beguilement and deception. The demon is adept at swaying the hearts of mortals.\nRemember that anything it may offer you is false. To the demon, you are merely prey.","done":"Not bad, ‹name›. Your have bested the fiend, and your will remains unbroken.\nMany a ‹class› has believed themselves strong enough to bind a sayaad, only to become the demon's next meal instead. I am pleased to see you are not so foolish.\nWatch closely, and I will teach you the invocation to call upon your newly bound incubus.\nStormwind City Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":25.4,"y":78.4,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4963":{"id":4963,"t":"Shard of an Infernal","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Infus Emerald and use it on one of the Infernals found in Desolace. After successful, bring the Infus Emerald and the Imprisoned Infernal Spirit back to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\nInfus Emerald\nImprisoned Infernal Spirit\nProvided: Infus Emerald","desc":"So, you have chosen to capture the soul of an infernal, good.\nTake this emerald--with it, you will be able to capture the creature's soul. It works very similar to spells you already know: when the creature is close to dying, use the gem and it should do the rest of the work for you.\nI would suggest going to Desolace and trying your hand at any of the infernals there. Those should do nicely.\nAfter you're successful, take both the captured spirit and your emerald to Menara.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"Yes, ‹name›? Have you chosen? Infernal or felhound?\nEach choice is personal and should reflect your strengths and weaknesses. It is not unheard of for a warlock to enhance themselves further instead of making up in areas they lack. Sometimes overpowering an enemy is just as strong a tactic than becoming a more balanced spell caster.","done":"Ah, the spirit of an infernal. Well done, ‹name›.\nWhen I have both the spirit and the cleansed orb, I will merge the two for you, but not until then.\nThe Barrens Desolace","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.2,"n":"Acolyte Magaz","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7603":{"id":7603,"t":"Kroshius' Infernal Core","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search Shatter Scar Vale in Felwood for the remains of Kroshius. When you locate the remains, use the Fel Fire near them and await Kroshius' return. When the infernal has awoken, slay him and take from his corpse Kroshius' Infernal Core.\nReturn Kroshius' Infernal Core to Niby the Almighty in Felwood.\nKroshius' Infernal Core Kroshius\nKroshius slain\nProvided: Fel Fire","desc":"Kroshius lays in a heap to the northeast, in the Shatter Scar Vale. Take this Fel fire and use it on his remains. The fire should reanimate the fallen infernal.\nAt this point, I fully expect him to kill you and your minion.\nIf by some miracle you happen to kill Kroshius, take his infernal core and return it to Niby.","rew":"You will receive:\nShard of the Green Flame\nYou will learn: Inferno\nExperience: 7,050","back":"Did you get lost?","done":"A deal is a deal! Quickly, take this and write this down. I don't have time! My greatest conjuration is upon us!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":41.6,"y":45.1,"n":"Niby the Almighty","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"94003":{"id":94003,"t":"The skybreaker bulwark","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Reclaim the Skybreaker Bulwark from Zaal Stormshield at the Shrine of Akir.\nSkybreaker Bulwark","desc":"I am all that remains of the line of Skybreakers here on Zephras Isle. The rest were murdered by the Al'Aketh.\nThe only thing that outweighs my sorrow is my shame. My family's ancestral shield--the Skybreaker Bulwark--is now in the hands of a cultist named Zaal Stormshield. Family lore holds no harm may befall a worthy wielder of this shield.\nZaal is not worthy, of that I am sure. Find this man at the Shrine of Akir and reclaim my shield from him. Do this and I will teach you the Skybreaker Defense.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormforged Protector\nExperience: 850\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"<Seena nods curtly at you.>","done":"You have done what I could not and restored my family honor. For this, I will bestow a gift that few on Zephras are worthy to receive. I will teach out the secrets of the Skybreaker Defense.\nAlso, you will need a shield to put what I have to teach you into practice. Please, take this one. I have little use for it now that the Skybreaker Bulwark has been returned to me.\nBanu'Adoraah, friend.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.8,"y":72.8,"n":"Seena Skybreaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1683":{"id":1683,"t":"Vorlus Vilehoof","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Horn of Vorlus to Elanaria in Darnassus.\nHorn of Vorlus Vorlus Vilehoof","desc":"Before I can teach you, you must show me your resolve.\nThe satyr Vorlus Vilehoof has found one of our remote moonwells, southeast of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. He now splashes within it, defiling its pure waters with his filth.\nFind Vorlus at the moonwell and destroy him. Bring me his horn as proof and I will begin your advanced training as a warrior.\nThe path to the moonwell is hidden well, ‹name›, but stay focused and alert and you will find it.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Do you have the horn, ‹name›? Is our moonwell free of the fiend Vorlus?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. It is good to know Vorlus is defeated and our moonwell cleansed, and it is good to see young warriors eager to keep our beloved Teldrassil free of corruption.\nNow let us begin your training...\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":57.3,"y":34.6,"n":"Elanaria","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1843":{"id":1843,"t":"Brutal Gauntlets","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrutal Gauntlets\nExperience: 1,850","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. These gauntlets are my best work. Take them. In wearing them, you bring honor to me and my ancestors.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.3,"y":74.3,"n":"Ula'elek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8403":{"id":8403,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"4883":{"id":4883,"t":"Guarding Secrets","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Nara Wildmane.\nBlue-feathered Necklace Berserk Owlbeast 50 % , Moontouched Owlbeast 50 % , Crazed Owlbeast 50 %\nProvided: Blue-feathered Necklace","desc":"While I do possess much knowledge about the owlbeasts you defeated in Winterspring, I am not very learned on the subject of the magics they wield. But I do believe I know of one that would be able to examine the necklace and most likely tell you what it is.\nNara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff is an expert in this field; see her. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSeaspray Bracers Shining Armplates\nExperience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"How may I help you, ‹name›?","done":"The energy of this necklace, ‹name›. I believe that it has only one source.\n<Nara closes her eyes and is quiet for a moment.>\nThe wildkin, now misguided and confused, were once not so. They once had a purpose, and were guided to serve. The night elf goddess Elune created these creatures to guard her most sacred areas.\nWhile this fact may seem like it holds little value; I urge you to look deeper.\nYou will learn, in time. Thank you for bringing this to me, ‹name›.\nFelwood Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.7,"y":52.8,"n":"Trull Failbane","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5123":{"id":5123,"t":"The Final Piece","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Crudely-written Log to Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\nCrudely-written Log High Chief Winterfall\nProvided: Crudely-written Log","desc":"The log you found on the high chief looks extensive, but after looking through a couple of the pages, you find that you cannot read the text. The markings are so crude and poorly-formed that you are not sure if anyone would be able to read them.\nBut perhaps Donova will be able to tell you what it says...","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"Now, what's this, ‹name›?","done":"I wonder what all of this means... I can't make anything out...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"4803":{"id":4803,"t":"Shardtooth E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Shardtooth E'ko Rabid Shardtooth 20 % , Elder Shardtooth 20 % , Shardtooth Bear 20 % , Shardtooth Mauler 20 %","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Ember","back":"In Winterspring, you will find large bears wit extremely thick hides. These Shardtooth bears gain much protection from what dey can withstand. If you wish ta gain the resistance against fire, bring me da E'ko you find from da Shardtooth.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92643":{"id":92643,"t":"The turncoat","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the cultist turncoat at the house just inside the highlands northwest of Valanaar.\nFind the secluded house in Shen'dar Highlands\nFind the Al'Aketh Turncoat","desc":"There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\nThis defector is hiding at a secluded residence just northwest of Valanaar inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, its worth some risk.","done":"<This man is clearly dead, killed by the assassins that you fought outside the house. As you kneel down to inspect the body you notice the glinting reflection of something shiny...>","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":56,"y":58.8,"n":"Dead Cultist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});